{ka broda} cannot mean "salty" etc. "ti ka silna" means "this is a property 
of being salt", not "this is salty". You could make lujvo like {silnyvu'i} 
etc. Replacing gismu by lujvo is also possible, but then I guess you want 
to use more meaningful terms for other things too, like {fetre'a} instead 
of {ninmu} and {nalma'u} instead of {verba} and {nalma'ufetre'a} instead of 
{nixli} and maybe even {cmuvla} instead of {gismu}...

mu'o mi'e ianek

